audio:
  lang: en
  lines:
    male|a||People with generous health insurance use far more medical care. Is that because care is cheap for them, or because people who expect big bills buy generous plans?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10880
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||Take two families, with numbers made up to keep it plain: the Lenas expect a knee operation, the Toms nothing much.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1hnsahi'
    male|a||With free care, the Lenas would spend three thousand dollars. Paying ninety-five percent of every bill, two thousand five hundred.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:11tfc4y'
    male|a||The Toms would spend six hundred with free care, and four hundred paying almost everything themselves.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:auuv9d'
    'male|a||So the price does matter: free care adds five hundred dollars for the Lenas and two hundred for the Toms.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1anj1ss'
    male|a||On average, three hundred and fifty dollars a family. That is the number we are after.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1t542t3'
    'male|a||But families choose their plans. Call the generous one D equals one: the Lenas, with the operation coming, choose it, and the Toms take the cheap one.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1n1qpt0'
    male|a||So we only ever see the Lenas with free care, and the Toms paying their own bills.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1k66knp'
    'male|a||Before the sum, a prediction. Compare what we can see: the Lenas'' spending minus the Toms''. How will that gap compare with the true three hundred and fifty?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:10n9aox'
    'male|a||Far above: the Lenas would spend a lot on any plan, so their bill carries the knee operation as well as the price.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8040
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||Three thousand against four hundred: a gap of two thousand six hundred dollars.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5000
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||Only five hundred of it is the price, the effect on the Lenas. The other two thousand one hundred is the operation, which they would pay for on any plan.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1ei2ys4'
    'male|a||That second piece is selection: it measures who buys generous cover, not what the cover does.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1ofotep'
    male|a||In general, the gap between plans is the effect on those who chose the generous one, plus how differently the two groups would spend on the same plan.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1e82zhr'
    male|a||No survey of insurance plans can pull the two apart, because a family's choice of plan already carries its own forecast of its bills.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:qcf5bg'
    male|a||Unless someone else chooses the plan, by lottery. Then the two groups would spend alike on the same plan, so the selection term falls to zero.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1adiw3x'
    male|a||And the gap between the plans becomes the average effect, the three hundred and fifty we were after.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:gnev3t'
    male|a||In the nineteen seventies, the RAND Corporation did exactly that.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:csnucd'
    male|a||RAND's experiment ran from 1974 to 1982, in six places from Dayton, Ohio, to Seattle, and enrolled about two thousand seven hundred and fifty families.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11760
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||Each family was given a plan by lot, for three or five years: free care, or paying twenty-five, fifty or ninety-five percent of every bill.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:9zwb6k'
    'male|a||But nobody faced ruin: a family''s payments for the year stopped at a share of its income, and never above a thousand dollars.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1k2gkuu'
    male|a||And families on the costlier plans were paid larger lump sums for joining, to make up for the bills they might face.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1uwm0t6'
    male|a||Why randomize a price, and not coverage itself? Because in the early seventies Congress was debating national health insurance, and the open question was how much patients should pay.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:7ly1bh'
    male|a||And a price comes in doses. Insured against uninsured gives one gap; four prices can trace a whole curve.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:az27lc'
    male|a||First, a guess. Compared with families paying ninety-five percent of every bill, how much more did free-care families spend?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1nakyy'
    'male|a||About forty-five percent more: a clear response to price, though far from a flood.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5280
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||Here are the results, per person per year, in 1991 dollars. Free care: about one thousand and twenty.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8800
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||Paying ninety-five percent: about seven hundred. So free-care families spent some forty-five percent more, a gap far too large to be chance.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:vozevx'
    'male|a||The twenty-five percent plan landed in between, at about eight hundred and twenty-five. The fifty percent plan was small, and its number is rough: one re-analysis even puts it above the twenty-five.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1nqrr6j'
    'male|a||Join them, and you have something economists usually have to assume: a demand curve for medical care, traced out by a lottery.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:fvwmpj'
    male|a||And it bends. Most of the fall comes in the first step, from free care to paying a quarter of the bill.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1x3nutk'
    male|a||Watch the point slide from free care toward the ninety-five percent plan, and see where spending falls fastest.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:jgmtbd'
    'male|a||Steep near zero, gentler after: going from free to a little changes more than going from a little to a lot, though the small middle plans cannot pin the shape down.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12440
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||RAND summed it up as a price elasticity of about minus zero point two: make care ten percent dearer, and people use about two percent less.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:121z18n'
    male|a||That number is RAND's modelled summary, not the slope of this curve. Simple calculations from the plan averages give anything from about minus zero point one to minus zero point five, and the cap made the real price lower than the coinsurance rate.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 16640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1nqdort'
    male|a||Where did the difference come from? Free care raised the share of people who used any care in a year from about seventy-six to ninety-three percent, and the share admitted to hospital from about eight to ten percent.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 12400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1qkphgf'
    male|a||The price acted on whether people started a course of care at all. Once they had, what that course cost barely moved.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:10gblk6'
    'male|a||One worry remains. The lottery chose the plans, but families chose whether to join, and whether to stay: of those offered free care, eighty-eight percent joined and finished; of those offered the ninety-five percent plan, sixty-three percent.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 16240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:pjljm2'
    male|a||In 2013, Aron-Dine, Einav and Finkelstein redid the numbers assuming the worst about who stayed away. Whether people used care at all still responded to price; how big the dollar drop was, and whether hospital use moved at all, became uncertain.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 16520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:iy7b7j'
    male|a||On free care, the share of people using any care in a year rose from about seventy-six to ninety-three percent, and the share admitted to hospital from about eight to ten percent. Did all that care buy better health?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 13200
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||RAND measured health as carefully as it measured bills: physical exams, blood tests and long questionnaires, at entry and again at the end.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1tj36q7'
    'male|a||The answer came in 1983, when Robert Brook''s team reported on almost four thousand people aged fourteen to sixty-one. The drawing shows direction, not scale: to the right means healthier on free care.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:oaw4zr'
    'male|a||General health, physical functioning, mental health: for the average participant, free care made no detectable difference.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1i1j14h'
    male|a||Nor did a calculated risk of dying.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 2840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:u8rjdf'
    male|a||And the ranges were tight. For the average participant, the authors could rule out anything more than a minimal effect, in either direction.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:s2z9gu'
    male|a||But two groups did gain. Low-income people with high blood pressure ended up with diastolic pressure about three millimetres of mercury lower on free care.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:n8n4zb'
    male|a||And people with poor eyesight saw a little better, by about a fifth of a line on the eye chart.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:o2pg00'
    male|a||For them, RAND's own summary projects about a tenth lower risk of early death. That is a projection from blood pressure, not a count of deaths.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:15m7rb1'
    male|a||A question RAND asked next. When a price made people use less care, which care did they give up?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:14p5lfy'
    'male|a||Both, about equally: cost sharing cut highly effective care about as much as care that rarely helps.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7680
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||So a price trims care bluntly: patients decide whether to go before anyone knows what is wrong.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6360
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||Yet most participants were working-age adults in fairly good health, with little that extra care could fix in three to five years.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1n4s986'
    male|a||The gains showed up where there was something to fix, with wider ranges, because those groups were small.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:whmkzn'
    male|a||So the average was flat, and the effects that did exist sat in a small corner of the sample, where the need was.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:nmxpke'
    'male|a||So here is the sentence people carry away from RAND: more care did not improve average health.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6440
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||It is often quoted as proof that medical care barely matters. Each of its words is narrower than that.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:tjv7du'
    male|a||More care means the extra visits that a zero price brought, among families who all had insurance of one kind or another.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:161nhsq'
    male|a||Did not improve means no change beyond a small margin, on these measures, over three to five years.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ujp6ba'
    'male|a||Average hides who gained: the poor with high blood pressure, and people with poor eyesight.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1yumsvg'
    'male|a||And health means the health of people aged fourteen to sixty-one who were able to work: none of the elderly, and no one was left uninsured.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:na70t0'
    'male|a||Economists still read the result two ways. RAND''s own team: for a typical adult, the extra care bought little measurable health, so moderate cost sharing saves money at small cost to health.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1b5lid1'
    male|a||Critics answer that even RAND's own data show the price cut effective care as much as useless care, that the poor and sick did lose, and that a few years is too short for heart disease or cancer to show.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 12520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1kdjuho'
    male|a||What would tell them apart is a much larger trial of people at high risk, followed for longer, or a trial among the uninsured.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1dffuwe'
    male|a||Oregon's 2008 lottery, which handed out Medicaid to uninsured low-income adults by drawing names, was a step that way.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:6q32v3'
    male|a||One new case. A state adds a copay for doctor visits for low-income adults, many with high blood pressure. Which reading of RAND fits?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:17gxyhg'
    male|a||Visits will fall, and these are the very people whose blood pressure free care lowered in RAND, so their control may slip.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8160
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||So why randomize the price of care? Because the price was the policy question, and a lottery of prices drew a demand curve that no comparison of chosen plans could.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 12320
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||Free care raised spending by about forty-five percent, mostly by bringing more people to start a course of care.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1l2wvhs'
    male|a||And the famous null holds for the average, fairly healthy adult at that margin, and breaks as soon as it is stretched to the poor and the sick.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:uouxgl'
    male|a||Read with every word attached, the sentence does not say that care doesn't matter. It says that a price is a blunt way to decide who gets it.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1inr70o'
    'male|a||Which family chose the generous plan: the one with a big bill coming, or the other?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5760
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||Yes.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 1120
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||Right.:
